 "title": "FINANCE OFFICE (Auditor/Treasurer) | perkinscounty",
 "text": "-->\nFINANCE OFFICE (Auditor/Treasurer) | perkinscounty\ntop of page\nSkip to Main Content\nHOME\nDEPARTMENTS\nDRIVER LICENSES\nCLERK OF COURTS\nDIRECTOR OF EQUALIZATION\nFINANCE OFFICE (Auditor/Treasurer)\nTAX DEEDS\nHIGHWAY\nREGISTER OF DEEDS\nSHERIFF/EMERGENCY MANAGEMENT\nSTATES ATTORNEY\nVETERANS OFFICE\nWEED AND PEST\nPREDATOR CONTROL\n4-H\nCOMMISSIONERS\n2026 Meeting Minutes\nLEGAL NOTICES\nGIS & PLAT MAP\nORGANIZED TOWNSHIP PORTAL\nELECTIONS\nPROPERTY TAX RELIEF PROGRAMS\nARCHIVE LEGAL NOTICES\nABOUT US\nJOB OPPORTUNITIES\nMORE PORTALS\nUse tab to navigate through the menu items.\nFinance Office\n(Auditor/Treasurer)\nPO Box 126\nBison, SD 57620\n605-244-5624 (Auditor phone)\n605-244-5613 (License & Tax Division phone)\n605-231-5560 (Fax)\nSara Stadler - Finance Officer\nAmanda Larson - Deputy Finance Officer\nBridget Keller - Deputy Finance Officer\nFor Election Page, click here\nThe County Finance Officer is the elected county business manager. He/she is responsible for commissioner proceedings, agendas and records, accounting records, revenue and expense reports, voter registration and elections. Businesses apply for beer and liquor licenses with the finance office.\nThe Finance Officer figures real estate and mobile home taxes, handles county bid lettings, indigent medical claims and collection of tax liens. The Finance Officer is also the collector of taxes, has the duty to receive all money belonging to the county, maintaining accounting records, payment of all county bills, and is responsible for county fund investment. Motor vehicle licensing, game licenses and drivers licenses are obtained at the finance office. The County Finance Officer also administers the county welfare program.\nDriver's Licensing\nDriver's License Test hours are:\n​\nMonday - Thursday 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m.\nFriday 8:00 a.m. - 11:30 a.m.\n​\nLocation: 100 East Main Street, Bison, SD\nFEE CHANGE\nDriver's License / ID Card $38.00\nCommercial Driver's License $43.00\nCDL Endorsement Tests $20.00\nDuplicate DL/ID $20.00\nSD Department of Public Safety\n​\nDepartment of Motor Vehicles Forms\nDriver's License and ID Card Information\nMust bring 2 pieces of mail with a current physical address, dated within the last year. Nothing hand written.\nNew/Out of state: Birth Certificate and Social Security, if federally compliant, birth certificate only along with the mail pieces\nIf you can't provide the required documents when you come, we will not be able to renew your driver's license or ID.\nProperty Tax\nProperty Tax Relief Programs\nForms For Towns/Townships\nTax Limitations and Opt Out Information for all taxing districts (except School Districts)\nTownship Annual Reports (PDF)\n​\nTownship Annual Report Fillable (Excel\n​\nOath of Office for Township Officers\n​\nTownship Officers and Levy Request\n​ ​ ​ ​\n​\n​\n2024 Payable 2025 Levies\n​\n2024 Payable 2025 Graphed Levies\n​\n​\nAnnual Report for 2025\nPerkins County Audit Report\nFor the Two Years Ended December 31, 2023\nbottom of page",
